body:
@AllenDowney good summary. pull-request?

I had meant that `df.a = 'foo'` _could_ translate to `df['a'] = 'foo'`, but then you would have to have a method `df.set_attribute('a2','foo')` that could then set an actual attribute. But on 2nd thought this is really a big change. So let's go with your summary.

I think an option for the warning is the best as it will happend EVERY time (unless you turn of the option entirely, and can be worked around by using `pd.option_context` to set the context
